+Various heuristics assist in determining whether colors should be enabled by default. Specifically, Loguru honors |the-no-color-environment-variable|_ and disables coloring if it is set to any value. Conversely, Loguru honors |the-force-color-environment-variable|_ and enables coloring if it is set to any value (this is useful for non-TTY environments that do support colors). Note that ``NO_COLOR`` takes precedence over ``FORCE_COLOR`` if both are set. Additionally, terminals identified by ``TERM=dumb`` are considered to lack color support.
 
 In any case, you can always control log coloring by explicitly specifying the ``colorize`` argument of the |add| method::
 
